  "question": {
    "text": "In the estimation of bromine, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></math> of an organic compound gave <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>40</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></math> of silver bromide. The percentage of bromine in the given compound is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>%</mo></math> (nearest integer)<br />(Relative atomic masses of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Ag</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Br</mi></math> are <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>108</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">u</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>80</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">u</mi></math>, respectively).",
    "image": null
  },
